          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Where Tool-Battery Propane Heaters Fit</h3>

          <p>
            Tool-battery propane heaters are the best fit when you need to warm a space and there is no outlet: a garage, a hunting blind, an ice-fishing shanty, a job site or, with the right indoor-rated model, a living room during an outage. Their weakness is fuel logistics and combustion safety. You need propane on hand, ventilation and a carbon monoxide alarm.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Where Wearables and Blankets Fit</h3>

          <p>
            Wearables and blankets are the best fit for keeping people comfortable in a cold house or car. They are silent, safe to use while sleeping and incredibly efficient. Their weakness is that the room stays cold, so pipes, pets and anyone not wearing one get no benefit. A power station with a heater sits in between: genuinely electric, genuinely battery powered, but limited to short bursts unless the battery is huge. Our <a href="/best-electric-space-heater/">electric space heater guide</a> covers the heaters themselves, including low-wattage models that pair best with a battery.
          </p>
