        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            A rechargeable battery heater that warms a room for hours does not exist at any sensible size or price, and products that claim otherwise are selling hand warmers with fans. The real answers are better: the DEWALT DXH12B gives you genuine room heat from propane with a tool battery running the fan and the safety shutoffs that allow careful indoor use, while the RYOBI and Milwaukee forced-air heaters handle garages and job sites.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For keeping people warm, nothing beats heating the person. An ORORO vest, OCOOPA hand warmers and a 12V heated blanket running off an EcoFlow DELTA 2 will keep a household comfortable through a long outage on a fraction of the energy a space heater would burn. Whatever you choose, if it burns fuel, put a carbon monoxide alarm next to it.
